      "side": 1,
      "message": "This test exercises that sequential / dependent command buffers work when submitted to the multiple queues sequentially. Could you also add a test that exercises 2 independent workloads being submitted to the different queues simultaneously?\n\n```\nTEST_P(GfxstreamEnd2EndVkTest, UseDoubleQueuesWithSimulatenousSubmit) {\n\u003cmake buffer 1\u003e\n\u003cmake buffer 2\u003e\n\n\u003cmake command buffer 1\u003e\n\u003cmake command buffer 2\u003e\n\n\u003crecord command buffer 1\u003e\n\u003crecord command buffer 2\u003e\n\nstd::barrier threadsReady(2);\n\nstd::thread thread1([\u0026]() {\n  // Wait for both threads to be \"running\" to try to catch behavior when \n  // submitting to the same underlying queue that is emulated by 2 virtual queues.\n  threadsReady.arrive_and_wait();\n  \n  \u003csubmit command buffer 1 to queue 1\u003e\n});\nstd::thread thread2([\u0026]() {\n  // Wait for both threads to be \"running\" to try to catch behavior when \n  // submitting to the same underlying queue that is emulated by 2 virtual queues.\n  threadsReady.arrive_and_wait();\n  \n  \u003csubmit command buffer 2 to queue 2\u003e\n});\n\nthread1.join();\nthread2.join();\n\n}\n```",
